body: "Implementation evidence (2026-08-07):\n- Upgraded pm CLI/SDK and pm-changelog contracts to 2026.8.7; lock resolution is current and npm audit reports zero vulnerabilities after brace-expansion 5.0.9.\n- Installed the canonical extension merge fence: generated extensions are non-mergeable while .managed-extensions.json retains pm-json semantic merging.\n- A fresh npm-installed pm 2026.8.7 tracker exposed that context-usage --format json returned host-default TOON. The command now returns an owned rendered JSON payload; behavior-driven tests cover local --format json, global --json, filters, missing ledgers, affinity, and graceful SDK-affinity failure.\n- Fresh acceptance at a disposable /tmp tracker installed this exact local extension, activated all three commands, packed a real item, parsed context-usage JSON, and passed strict check-only health with no warnings.\n- Exact coverage: 195 tests passed; lines 100%, branches 100%, functions 100% across all three runtime source files.\n- npm and Bun release gates, package dry-run, changelog check, dependency freshness, and npm production/full audits pass.\n- Full vector health without --check-only is separately tracked upstream in pm-cli#928; the silent Ollama wait reproduced under a 45-second bound and fresh evidence was added without duplicating the issue.\n- Publication remains maintainer-gated and was not attempted.\n\nPrivacy evidence addendum:\n- The changed patch and tracked working tree contain no secret signatures, host addresses, or absolute host paths under the package privacy pattern scan.\n- Reachable commit metadata still contains one legacy personal-domain identity class. This is not introduced by this patch and does not block merging the package fix, but it blocks publication approval; remediation is tracked separately in pm-context-r6x0 because rewriting shared public history requires explicit maintainer coordination.\n\nReview handoff:\n- PR #54 opened from commit e0e22c1. Exact-head automated review will begin after this PM-link commit so all reviewers inspect the complete evidence state."
